WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
In Belfast, the Titanic Quarter surrounds
the very place where Titanic was designed,

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.030
built and launched.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.970
Old docks like these are brownfield land.

4
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.790
Today they host a visitor
attraction and a hotel.

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.310
Worldwide, about 60 per cent of land turned
urban since 1970 was formerly productive

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.410
farmland.

7
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:26.030
And built-up area per person
rose from 43 to 63 square metres.

8
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.230
So why would a city build
on old, polluted land,

9
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.810
when empty fields lie next door?

10
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.210
Is it just cheaper?

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.590
In this mission, you'll
cross the rural–urban fringe,

12
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.150
from inner city to commuter village.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.930
Then you'll judge each
kind of site on economic,

14
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.530
social and environmental grounds.

15
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.910
Your mission: decide when building on
old factory land is the more sustainable

16
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.870
choice.
